From 5c304a077c257459d0551ae2ac292d10e1558db3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:35:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] What we've learned v2: its own page, removable leans, Less of
 on Pitch, the menu row (rules 1780-1783)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Settings › Tune for you's first row previews the first four chips (+N) or "Rate N more to see what we've
learned" and pushes the page (web ProfileMenu view "learned", iPhone LearnedScreen replacing LearnedDrawer);
the menu's Tuned for you row is now an always-on "What we've learned" under Settings with its count and dot;
the Taste tab links to it under Film DNA. The page: a Bodoni template summary, What you're into (strands,
directors, languages, eras, genres, told-us chips), Near your taste, + Add, Less of this (Never and soft,
fading skips), Also tuning your picks, and the Sharpen gate under 15 rated.

Removing a lean puts its id in viewingPrefs.learnedOff: "Your kind of films" stops leaning on it
(effectiveKind), else 4 rank points (8 max) on films carrying it; adding goes to kind or a new boost list.
Never the match % or Film DNA. Pitch now reads stored avoid (hard) and notMine (soft x0.75), an explicit
ask overriding either. Pitch battery 170/170 -> 176/176, existing rows identical; test-recut-rank identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
