+- **Before → after (Picks, Tonight, every ranked list):** What we've learned could only mute a film chip (`chip:` in learnedOff, rule 1570's `learnedPoints`). Now it also takes leans: `strand:`, `person:`, `lang:`, `era:`, `genre:`. A muted lean held by "Your kind of films" is taken out of the kind for every reader (`effectiveKind`: the genre lean of up to 6 points, the era mix, the chosen-language swap among the reveal's three, the "Sometimes" subtitle lean), so that exact boost stops. Any other muted lean costs a film that carries it 4 rank points, 8 at most (`MUTE_POINTS`, `MUTE_CAP`; a strand is carried at a label reading of 60+ by `strandValue9`, a person by the candidate's `directors`, a language by `original_language`, an era by year). An added lean goes into kind where it fits (a genre under five picked, a kind era, a language) or into the new `viewingPrefs.boost`, which lifts a film that carries it 4 points, 8 at most. Rank points only, through `withSkips` / `demotionOf` / `skipRankPoints`; the match % and the Film DNA chart (dnaLift, dna-labels) do not read learnedOff or boost. `prefsKey` now carries the leans (`leansKey`), so saved picks rebuild on a change.
+- **Before → after (Pitch):** Pitch read no stored viewingPrefs. Now `avoid` is hard (`pitchAvoids`: the film never ranks, so bad it's good included) and `notMine` soft (`pitchLessOf`: score × `W_LESS_OF` 0.75), each lifted by the ask: a genre, decade or years, Long, a language or a scary feel asked lifts the matching soft kind (`pitchChose`, the Chose rules Tonight and Browse use); violence asked up (gory, bloody, brutal) lifts Graphic gore, Graphic violence, War violence and Torture, scares up lifts Jump scares (`pitchAskedWarnings`). Tonight already kept both (fitsViewingPrefs hard on avoid, withSkips soft on notMine): unchanged.
+- **Why:** owner-approved 2026-11-12 (b69-what-weve-learned-v2.png frames b to f): removing a chip must actually stop Picks leaning on it while Film DNA stays the same; Less of: content is hard, everything else soft, and an explicit Pitch ask wins.
+- **Why 4 and 8:** the size of one "Your kind of films" genre lean (`KIND_LEAN_POINTS` 4, `KIND_LEAN_MAX` 6), below one Show less of step (10). The taste model's own pull toward a strand, a director, a language or an era lives inside the match %, which this never changes, so a mute leans back by about one kind lean rather than removing that pull. That is an approximation, said plainly on the page ("Picks will stop leaning on X") and here: not measured against a person's real picks.
+- **Measured:** pitch battery (signed out, fixture of 2026-11-04 with cult.txt) 170/170 before, 176/176 after; the 170 existing rows' markdown output is byte-identical before and after (no prefs are passed, and the fixture's new stand-in "musical" keyword on Music-genre films that are not documentaries changes none of them). Six new "less of" cases: with stored Graphic violence, films carrying it in the top 10 of "a horror movie" 3 → 0 and "a war movie" 8 → 0, while "a gory horror movie" still shows them (The Substance, The Thing, I Saw the Devil lead); with stored Musicals, "a musical" still answers with Music films (Whiplash, Sound of Metal, The Sound of Music) and "a romantic movie from the 60s" has 1 → 0 in the top 10 (still in the list: soft); with stored Animation, "an animated movie" still leads with The Lion King and Spider-Verse. On the same fixture "a feel-good romance" had 2 → 0 musicals in the top 24. scripts/test-recut-rank.ts output identical before and after (its one dial miss, "a scary movie that isn't too violent", is on main too). The lean points are checked by unit cases in check-invariants (1781): a muted strand on a slow, heavy film 4, three muted leans capped at 8, a boosted era −4, a muted kind genre 0 (its kind lean stops instead). Not measured: any real account's Picks before and after a mute, and the model-parse path of Pitch.
+- **Who it affects / data touched:** anyone who removes or adds a lean on What we've learned (new keys in public_profiles.result_json.viewingPrefs: learnedOff gains lean ids, `boost` is new; JSON, no migration), and every signed-in Pitch of someone with Things I'd rather avoid or Show less of set. No stored data rewritten.
